You are likely right that code chunking/retrieval needs improvement, but the evidence also shows a ranking problem.

Confirmed
ModelRunner CUDA graph question: the gold source is not in the top 10 retrieved chunks.
FlashInfer prepare question: the gold source is also not in the top 10.
Custom allreduce, FP8, Falcon: the gold source or overlapping chunk is retrieved.
So the code corpus is only problematic for some queries, especially exact method/function names.

Why it is mostly code chunking-related
The code chunker:

Splits files by Python function/class boundaries.
Creates fragments from long definitions at 2,000 characters.
Adds symbol names and signatures to the BM25 search document.
Still ranks only by BM25 terms.
This is less reliable for questions asking about two conditions inside a long function:

Multiple similar model_runner.py functions compete.
Multiple flashinfer.py methods compete.
The exact gold function may fall outside the top 10 because nearby symbols share many terms.
This is chunk ranking and code chunk precision, rather than a broken Python chunk parser.

Recommended fixes
Include AST definition names and parent class context more strongly in BM25.
Preserve one complete chunk for important small and medium functions instead of splitting unnecessarily.
Add neighboring code chunks as context when a retrieved function is split.
Experiment with top-3/top-5 code chunks instead of top-10.
Increase code-specific symbol matching, especially:
CudaGraph
prefill_meta
is_profile_run
use_aiter_and_is_supported
tie_word_embeddings
The Falcon, FP8, and custom-allreduce failures should improve mainly through generation. The ModelRunner and FlashInfer failures need better code retrieval first.